  user_2,[00:00] Hi Rahul, this is Ramesh from Safe Shield Agency, how can I help you today?
  user_1,[00:12] Uh, hi Ramesh... yeah, I wanted to double‑check that my auto policy AU‑45219 is really cancelled and… uh… expired now.
  user_2,[00:25] Sure thing, let me pull it up… [typing]… Yeah, I see the cancellation was processed on 25/09/2026 and the system now shows the policy status as **Expired**.
  user_1,[00:40] Okay… great. And the refund you mentioned in the chat – the ₹4,500 – when will that actually hit my account? I’m a bit worried it might get delayed.
  user_2,[01:00] No worries, the refund is queued and should reflect in your bank within 5‑7 business days. We’ll also email you the refund receipt as soon as it’s done.
  user_1,[01:15] Got it… Do I need to send back any paperwork or sign anything else? My car’s sold, so I just want to close everything cleanly.
  user_2,[01:30] Nope, you’re all set. The cancellation receipt we sent you over email is the only document you need to keep. The policy is officially expired, so there’s nothing else on your end.
  user_1,[01:45] Alright, thanks for confirming… and for the help. I’ll keep an eye on my account for the refund. Bye.
  user_2,[01:55] You’re welcome, Rahul. If anything else comes up, just give us a call. Have a good day!